      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BEYOND PERFECTION (3) is the clear horse with upside after putting away a Dubbo Mdn with ease first-up. He was held up early in the straight but let down sharply once finding the clear. Suspect he's got plenty more to offer and is one to follow. BONOYSTER (6) looks the immediate danger. He's knocking on the door and should be near his top now but is fairly exposed and needs to break a long drought. IT STAYS IN VEGAS (1) wasn't far away when resuming and is sure to be better with that run under his belt. Has good tactical speed and gets help at the weights again with the 3kg claimer sticking. Can give a sight. CHICKEN LEGS (4) is a credible danger after missing narrowly at Narromine when slow away and held up, and his broader 1000m record keeps him in the discussion.",
